ActivateItem "/BackGroundLayer/district/hoek"

// code 5: dmfnGeneral.miDefaultView.Click => PopupMenu."Default View"
DefaultView
WAIT 1000

// let classBreaks compute, WMS tiles download, and MapControl::UpdateView populate the layer
// control. 100 ms was not enough: the layer control was often not populated yet, so every SEND
// below was dropped -- WmCopyData silently returns when there is no active QDmsViewArea.
WAIT 5000

// Send cmd 4 (WM_COPYDATA->MdiChild) => ActiveDataView.ActiveControl.PopupMenu."Edit Palette"
// code 1 activates the popup menu on the active control. A quoted element names a menu item by the
// left part of its caption instead of by its position, so entries added or removed above it do not
// silently make this fire something else; a name that matches nothing, or matches more than one
// item, is reported as an error.
SEND 4 2 1 "Edit Palette"
// the palette editor is created through PostGuiOper, so it is not up on return
WAIT 3000

CascadeSubWindows // mdi_area->cascadeSubWindows()
WAIT 1000

TileSubWindows // mdi_area->tileSubWindows()
WAIT 1000

// code 0 (activate sub-object) with sequence {4}: the Numeric Class Count control of the Palette Editor => ActiveDataView.Activate(4);
SEND 4 2 0 4
WAIT 1000

// Send cmd 3 (WM->ActiveMdiChild) => AciveDataView.SendMsg(258, 52, 0);
// 258=WM_CHAR, 52='4'
SEND 3 3 258 52 0
WAIT 1000

// 256=WM_KEYDOWN, 13=VK_RETURN => AciveDataView.SendMsg(256, 13, 0);
SEND 3 3 256 13 0
WAIT 1000

// activate popup menus on active control of MdiChild.
// JenksFisher non-zero on purpose: it is the classification that runs on worker threads
// (CreateNonzeroJenksFisherBreakAttr), so the captured map view exercises that path rather than
// the trivial Equal Counts one. What the old numeric {1 2} fired here had drifted anyway.
SEND 4 3 1 "Classify" "JenksFisher non-zero"
// JenksFisher runs on worker threads; let it finish before the palette is read out
WAIT 5000

// activate the sub-object with sequence {6 1 1 3}: EditPalette/TableView/ScrollPort/TableHeader/3rdColum
SEND 4 5 0 6 1 1 3
WAIT 1000

// Index {7} was documented here as "Copy Palette", an item that no longer exists; the position has
// been firing Remove classBreaks instead. Named now, so the script says what it actually does.
SEND 4 2 1 "Remove classBreaks"
WAIT 1000

WAIT 5000

// Copy MapView viewport contents to clipboard (TB_Copy = 18)
SEND 3 2 273 18
WAIT 3000

// Send cmd 1 (WM->Main) 16 represents WM_CLOSE.
SEND 1 3 16 0 0
